From e3b4e2116c4bf4408555cb288d960a11be89b390 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 09:47:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] target/dadao: restore precise env->pc before raising an
 exception (ML-003b)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

dadao_raise_exception() only set exception_index and called
cpu_loop_exit() — env->pc still held whatever a prior branch/TB-boundary
write last set it to (only branch-family instructions and, since
ML-003f, DISAS_TOO_MANY write env->pc; a mid-TB helper-raised exception
like gen_exception_illegal's checks never did). do_interrupt() then
reported the wrong faulting address: the TB's entry PC, not the actual
instruction that failed a spec constraint check.

Fix: call cpu_restore_state(cs, pc) with the helper's return address
(GETPC()) before setting exception_index, mirroring what
dadao_cpu_do_unaligned_access already does for unaligned accesses.
helper_raise_exception now passes GETPC() through instead of 0.

Found while debugging an ILLI fault during picolibc printf (ML-003b):
the previously-reported PC pointed at vfprintf's entry (a harmless
`addi`), which was misleading; with this fix the debug build correctly
reported the actual faulting instruction. This is a general debugging
correctness fix independent of that specific investigation — any future
DADAO exception (ILLI/MALIGN) now reports where it really happened.

Verified: E2E 27/27, differential AGREE(4-way)=200/DIVERGE=0, no
regression.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 target/dadao/helper.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/target/dadao/helper.c b/target/dadao/helper.c
index 3e2aa39..5afc31d 100644
--- a/target/dadao/helper.c
+++ b/target/dadao/helper.c
@@ -10,13 +10,24 @@ G_NORETURN void dadao_raise_exception(CPUDADAOState *env,
                                       uintptr_t pc)
 {
     CPUState *cs = env_cpu(env);
+    /* Reconstruct the precise env->pc of the instruction that raised the
+     * exception (mid-TB helper call) — without this, env->pc still holds
+     * whatever a prior branch/TB-boundary write last set it to, and
+     * do_interrupt() reports the wrong faulting address (a debugging
+     * pitfall found via ML-003b: reported PC was the TB's *entry*, not
+     * the actual instruction, since gen_exception_illegal-style checks
+     * fire mid-block).
+     */
+    if (pc) {
+        cpu_restore_state(cs, pc);
+    }
     cs->exception_index = exception;
     cpu_loop_exit(cs);
 }
 
 void helper_raise_exception(CPUDADAOState *env, uint32_t exception)
 {
-    dadao_raise_exception(env, exception, 0);
+    dadao_raise_exception(env, exception, GETPC());
 }
 
 void helper_exit(CPUDADAOState *env, uint64_t code)
-- 
